From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:23:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a Chat upstream's [DONE] ends a translated reply's
 read, not its hangup (#5936)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A relay that streams a reply whole, says it over (finish_reason, [DONE])
and holds the connection kept the client waiting on the translated
reply's end: the read went on, the end was said only when the reading
gave up, and the client — Codex on a Chat-only provider, its turn stuck
in progress — gave up first. The reply now ends at the [DONE] its
protocol says it over with, its usage in the chunks before it; a reply
that said nothing is still the empty reply's to answer, and an upstream
whose end is told by its finish_reason (Gemini's OpenAI-compatible,
Command Code) is read as it was.

Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
